    answer: `Filter both time axes. A reference is: SELECT metric_id, dimension_key, metric_value, source_version FROM metric_history WHERE valid_from <= :business_as_of AND :business_as_of < COALESCE(valid_to, 'infinity'::timestamp) AND recorded_from <= :report_run_at AND :report_run_at < COALESCE(recorded_to, 'infinity'::timestamp). Business-valid time answers when the value applies; recorded time answers when the platform knew that version. Enforce non-overlap for each metric/dimension on both axes or rank only as a defensive diagnostic and fail the quality check. Index or physically organize around metric_id, dimension_key and the interval starts, retain immutable corrections, and persist both timestamps with every generated answer so an old report can be reconstructed exactly.`,
